{"activity_text": "Anti-Gram-", "article_id": "", "assay_text": "CD", "assay_type": "", "comments_text": "Sequence analysis: APD analysis reveals that this sequence is similar (81.82%) to cd4(Q5K,D9K) K=R: 19%, G: 16%, I: 13%. Designed by changing Q22 to K and D26 to A in KR-12 followed by connecting two copies of KR-12 with CPGG and GPGG. Activity: active against E. coli (MIC 0.312 uM) and P. aeruginosa (MIC 0.625 uM) in 10 mM tris buffer. Warning: other bacteria not tested. Structure: random coil in water and helical in lysoPG (78%). Peptide stability: CD4-PP gained stability to S. aureus protease aureolysin (~20% detected after 6 h), while the control LL-37 was nearly completely degraded in 1 h.", "concentration": "", "cytotoxicity_text": "", "hemolytic_activity_text": "", "measure_group": "", "measure_value": "", "pubmed_id": "35821354", "record_granularity": "entry_text", "reference_text": "Cell Mol Life Sci. 2022 Jul 11;79(8):411. doi: 10.1007/s00018-022-04440-w. PubMed", "sequence_key": "APD6:AP04667", "source_id": "AP04667", "source_numeric_id": "04667", "source_path": "APD6/apd6_export/structured/peptides.csv", "source_record_id": "AP04667", "source_table": "peptides.csv", "stability_text": "", "subject_name": "", "target_organism_text": "", "title": "A stable cyclized antimicrobial peptide derived from LL-37 with host immunomodulatory effects and activity against uropathogens.", "unit": "", "﻿database": "APD6"}
